A||||4||Raydar||Torque converter / Engine swap question||||1||
Z||000000||Raydar||09-29-2001||02:42 PM||||In the past, I've heard of drag racers using Vega (or similar) torque converters behind V-8s, for a higher stall speed.<P>How does the stall speed of the 4 cylinder torque converter compare to the one for the V-6? (This is assuming they're not the same part.)<P>I was considering the possibility of using the 4 cylinder converter behind the V-6 when I do my swap, for a little more torque multiplication. Might enable me to use a higher rear gear ratio (like the 4 banger's 2.84) and still have <I>some</I> standing-start acceleration. <BR>Once the TCC is locked in, it shouldn't make any diference on the highway at all. <P>Anybody know anything about this?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dumba$$||09-29-2001||03:01 PM||||just did this 2 weeks ago,<BR>before we put my rebilt 2.8 with a few goodys back in, we put a convertor in from a 4cyl corsica!<BR>deffinatly made a diff.<BR>it kinds of feels (slushy) during normal driving<BR>but when you nail it  you can tell <BR>it launches alot better<P><BR>but we also used a  stock 3.4 cam  so i dont know what that did (help or hurt ) the low rpm's  but it deff. helped the upper rpm's <P><BR>i say, do it!!  i like it <P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>4.9 caddy engine for sale 30,000 miles complete with bubba joes mounts!!  $850<P>if it dont go, put a fart can, and clear taillights on it!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dumba$$||09-29-2001||03:03 PM||||it's the same on the highway as before||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||09-29-2001||05:11 PM||||There's a torque convertor rebuilding co. in Philadelphia called Pat's.If you give him all the specs on the car such as drivetrain,weight,cam,gearing,etc.He gives you the proper stall speed.I'm sure there are many such companies around the country.He did the convertor thats going my 88 between the 3800SC and the 95 Pontiac van trans.He changed the van convertor to SC specs.||||reg||1
